From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the shell and apps start workers from their own
 files

The browser fetches a dedicated or shared worker's main script itself,
through the factories
`RegisterNonNetworkWorkerMainResourceURLLoaderFactories` returns, not
the page's. domicile:// was not among them, so every worker the shell
or an app started aborted with net::ERR_ABORTED while fetch() of the
same file worked.

- `ChromeContentBrowserClient::RegisterNonNetworkWorkerMainResourceURLLoaderFactories`
  adds `ShellURLLoaderFactory`, which serves a file only to its own
  origin (`MayReadFiles`).
- A worker's own imports already go through
  `RegisterNonNetworkSubresourceURLLoaderFactories` (patch 0008).

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index a893213..27f9c93 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -6640,6 +6640,14 @@ void ChromeContentBrowserClient::
   CHECK(browser_context, base::NotFatalUntil::M163);
   CHECK(factories, base::NotFatalUntil::M163);
 
+  // Domicile's engine fork. The browser fetches a worker's main script itself,
+  // through these factories rather than the page's, so without domicile://
+  // here every worker the shell or an app starts aborts while fetch() of the
+  // same file works. ShellURLLoaderFactory serves it only to its own origin.
+  factories->emplace(
+      domicile::kDomicileScheme,
+      domicile::ShellURLLoaderFactory::Create(DomicileShellRoot()));
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || \
     BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
   if (content::AreIsolatedWebAppsEnabled(browser_context) &&
